<header><h1>Gravity Rift: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/R_gravity_rift">Gravity Rift</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2>Notes</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Moving into a gravity rift, usually when it is the active system, will not provide the +1, nor will the ships have to roll for removal.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do gravity rifts work: when do I get +1 move and when do I roll?&rdquo;: &ldquo;A ship that stops in a rift gains nothing and doesn&rsquo;t roll until it later leaves.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A ship removed by a gravity rift is not destroyed.<sup>2,10</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>10</sup> Codex I: &ldquo;units that fail to survive the roll are removed from the board and returned to players&rsquo; reinforcements rather than being destroyed.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When a carrier leaves a gravity rift &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Units lost this way are removed rather than destroyed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>All ship movement must be declared before any of them roll for gravity rift removal. A player may not choose additional ships to move after seeing the result of this roll.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do ships move one at a time, and can I wait to see gravity rift rolls before moving others?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; you declare every moving ship and they move together; rift rolls come after.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 41.2: &ldquo;one die is rolled immediately before it exits the gravity rift system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The retreating player must declare which, if any, fighters and ground forces they are moving, and which ships will be transporting them. If they have the Fighter II technology, then for each fighter, they must choose if that fighter is moving itself or being transported.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When a carrier leaves a gravity rift, do the fighters and ground forces it carries roll too?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Declare which ship carries what before rolling.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a ship moves through or out of multiple gravity rifts, and/or the same gravity rift multiple times, each instance will provide a +1 to movement, and requires a separate roll for removal.<sup>1,2,8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do gravity rifts work: when do I get +1 move and when do I roll?&rdquo;: &ldquo;gets +1 move for that path, one per rift &hellip; Each ship that leaves or passes through a rift rolls.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR quick reference: &ldquo;Each Ship Moving Through or Out of Applies +1 Move and Rolls 1 die.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook quick reference: the same text.</li>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: <sup>6</sup> Partial conflict: RAW on moving through the same rift twice: &ldquo;the movement bonus is once per ship per tactical action, the negative roll requirement remains per time a ship moves out of or through a gravity rift.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a ship with capacity would transport another unit after moving out of or through a gravity rift, but is removed, that unit remains where it is.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 95.1b: &ldquo;Units being transported by a ship that is removed from the board by a gravity rift are also removed from the board.&rdquo; Units not yet picked up are not being transported.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A system containing a <a href="/F_vuilraith">Vuil&rsquo;raith</a> <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Dimensional%20Tear">Dimensional Tear</a> is an anomaly.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> &ldquo;Are systems that contain Vuil&rsquo;raith Cabal&rsquo;s Dimensional Tears anomalies? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do Vuil&rsquo;raith ships roll for Cormund&rsquo;s gravity rift &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;it is simply a gravity rift, and counts as an anomaly for objectives.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>All units moving into, through or out of anomalies must follow the same rules as ships moving into, through or out of anomalies.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> On Sardakk N&rsquo;orr&rsquo;s commander: the LRR &ldquo;Will also prevent units from being committed to planets in anomalies without the appropriate technology.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
</article>
